Z||000003||kslish||06-18-2001||12:05 AM||||MooCow...did Ed happen to mention what he charges for the 4.9L swap?  I have a garage storing an '86SE for me that needs an engine (still waiting for the salvage title from the state).  I've been considering the 4.9L swap but won't have the time to attempt it myself until probably at least next summer (I've got too many progects on my other two Fieros to get finished this year).  Towing it to Ed's may be a reasonable solution if it fits into my budget....<P><P>------------------<BR>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR>See them at <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html</A><BR>Western PA Fiero Club - <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jay in Atlanta||06-18-2001||10:29 AM||||Just back from the Fiero Factory myself, where my wife and I picked up our new red '85 SE 5-speed on Saturday.  Ed's a heck of a guy, and he's got some great cars around.  I too got to see the Taz 3800 and talk to Ed about the 4.9 swap.  He says it adds so little weight (especially in comparison to the 3800) that it's a near perfect option.  I also got to drive his '85 SE 3.4 conversion, and loved the acceleration on that thing.  Ed (and the Fiero Factory) rules!!!<P>~Jay<BR>red '85 SE 5-Speed||||reg||10
Z||000005||Songman||06-18-2001||11:38 AM||||I didn't think Ed does the 4.9 swaps. Taz did his own car.....<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jay in Atlanta||06-18-2001||01:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>I didn't think Ed does the 4.9 swaps. Taz did his own car.....<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Taz's car is still a 3800 that he did himself; but he and Ed were there working together on the 4.9--they were talking about the details while I was there.  Ed does want to see if he can do it practically as a mass conversion for us nuts.<P>Also, MooCow, Ed said he was highly interested in putting together a 4.9 kit.  I can see that the welding would be a problem, but he was still trying to look for ways around it and see if it could be put out as a kit.  Maybe, maybe not.  Either way, Ed is very interested in trying to make this a standard conversion.<P>~Jay<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Jay in Atlanta||06-18-2001||02:49 PM||||Hey, here's the final word (for now) on Ed's 4.9 conversion.  This is off of the Yahoo group, from Ed himself:<P>"Sammy, and all, we are really NOT offering a 4.9 Cadillac conversion. At<BR>least not at this time, and maybe never.<P>We are slowly, very slowly, attempting to develop a kit that we hope will<BR>allow a 1 week installation time at a reasonable price. Regardless of<BR>whether the Fiero is 84-87, 88, manual trans, or auto. If this time frame<BR>cannot be realized at the shop, then we will only offer the specialized<BR>parts for DIY.<P>We do have 5 new 4.9's at the shop that will be installed. But they are<BR>for folks that are providing their time, knowledge, resources, $$'s, and<BR>long waiting periods to see if this can be accomplished. By taking this<BR>approach, shop time is very little and that will hold down overall<BR>development costs and ultimately the prices of any "kit" that may result.<BR>Just takes longer, lots longer, then devoting shop time to this project.<P>To give you an idea of what is involved: custom mounting brackets that<BR>bolt to any year<BR>Fiero cradle and use "off the shelf" mounts for the engine, custom<BR>brackets that mount "off the shelf" belt tensioners and idler pulleys,<BR>"off the shelf" axles and trans mount brackets for auto's or specially<BR>made flywheels and clutches for manual trans, "off the shelf" control<BR>cables, "off the shelf" coolant connections, custom made a/c manifold<BR>lines, a custom built exhaust system that will bolt up to a stock Fiero<BR>one, and finally a custom "plug and play" wiring harness or at least<BR>instructions of how you modify one.<P>And... keep all this within a reasonable price and time frame and with<BR>easy access for future service.<P>Think that anyone that has "crossbred" an engine (except a 3.4) would<BR>agree that we are attempting the impossible to accomplish within the 1<BR>week time frame.<P>Hope this will lay to rest all the rumors. These are the facts of the<BR>matter.<P>Ed Parks...from: The Fiero Factory<BR>8710B Hwy 53<BR>Toney, Ala 35773<BR>Days: 256-420-5391   Nights 256-882-1568 <A HREF="http://www.welcome.to/thefierofactory"" TARGET=_blank>http://www.welcome.to/thefierofactory"</A> <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||jch82||06-18-2001||07:10 PM||||Here's a few pics from our little adventure to the Fiero Factory.....<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/IM000032.JPG">   <BR>3.4 Turbo<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/IM000035.JPG">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/IM000043.JPG">  <BR>Taz 3.8<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/IM000044.JPG">  <BR>Taz 3.8<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/IM000050.JPG">  <BR>3.4 Turbo<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/IM000060.JPG">  <BR>4.9 Caddy<P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I><P>[This message has been edited by jch82 (edited 06-18-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by jch82 (edited 06-18-2001).]||||reg||1
